## Slide 3

In their own words

WHAT PEOPLE AROUND THEM SAY

69%

said fire alarms are important, but people ignore them.

23% said everyone should have one. 8% said they are too costly.

RELIABILITY

“It might not work when we actually need it.”

SLEEPING RISK

“Not knowing there is a fire when I'm sleeping.”

HIGH FLOORS

“I'm on a high floor and it's difficult to get down because the lifts can't be used.”

MAINTENANCE

“Not maintained, costly, and needs regular checks.”

LOUDNESS

“Some of them don't have loud alarms.”

AFFORDABILITY

“We don't have one here. Please make it affordable.”

Quotes are lightly edited for spelling and translated from Hinglish. Answers such as “idk” and blanks are left out.

