## Slide 4

Who is affected, and what they need

Stakeholder
Role
Needs
Concerns
Residents and hostel students
Primary
Warning even while asleep; a clear alarm; a known exit route.
Cost, false alarms, a device that fails when needed.
Families and home owners
Primary
Safety of family and property; easy, low-cost setup.
Affordability, battery changes, upkeep.
Wardens, PG and building managers
Primary
Monitor many rooms; simple testing and maintenance.
Maintenance load, nuisance-alarm complaints, liability.
Fire services and responders
Secondary
A fast, accurate alert that shows where the fire is.
Late calls, false calls, unknown location.
Authorities and regulators (fire dept, BIS and NBC)
Secondary
Compliance with fire-safety codes; fewer fire deaths.
Unreliable or non-standard devices.
Makers, installers and suppliers
Secondary
A simple, low-cost product that is easy to install.
Part cost, reliability, after-sales support.

