## Slide 5

Why sustainability matters here

Sustainability
The ability to maintain or support a process ,system ,or resources continuously over a long period of time without depleting or destroying it .

1

Early warning
Detects smoke, flame and heat before a fire spreads

2

Low cost
Built under the ₹1,500 limit (about ₹1,480)

3

Reusable parts
Most components can be reused or recycled

## Slide 6

SDGs followed by our fire alarm

SDG 3

Good Health and Well-being
Reduces injuries and deaths from fire and smoke inhalation

SDG 9

Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure
Promotes sensor and IoT-style technology

SDG 11

Sustainable Cities and Communities
Makes homes, colleges, offices and public buildings safer

SDG 13

Climate Action
Limits fire spread, cutting greenhouse gas release

## Slide 7

Components used in Fire Alarm System

COMPONENTS
RECYCLABLE  OR NON-RECYCLABLE
Arduino Uno
YES (Reuse the Board in another electronics project)
MQ-2 Gas and smoke sensor 
YES(The  stainless  steel mesh cover and outer housing can be melted down and recycled as scrap metal.
IR Flame sensor module 
No
DHT11 Temperature Sensor
YES
ACTIVE BUZZER
YES (We can use it in alarm and notification system)
5V Single relay module 
YES(Some parts like electromagnetic copper coil,silver contact points) 
5V  DC Fan
YES(Can be used in small Ventilation projects)
16x2 12C LED Display
YES 
HC 05 Bluetooth module 
YES(If it is functional we can use it in robotics projects)
220kΩ resistors
YES (if it is working  we can reuse it)
Bread Board and Jumper wires
Usually 

## Slide 8

Impact of a sustainable system

Environment

Low-power components keep electricity use small
Faster response can limit fire spread and release of smoke and harmful gases
Smoke-extracting fan clears smoke from the room

Human health

Early detection lowers risk of fire injuries and deaths
Smoke particles and gases harm the lungs; early evacuation reduces inhalation
Four alert levels cut false alarms, so people trust the alarm

## Slide 9

Our approach: reduce, reuse, recycle, dispose

1

Reduce

Only 3 sensors and a few actuators; low-power parts

2

Reuse

Parts are removable, so they go into the next project

3

Recycle

Metal parts and relay contacts go to scrap recovery

4

Dispose

Non-recyclable parts go to e-waste collection, not the bin

